; P6.2 exit-gate carrier: @key-bearing co-recursion with a NON-VACUOUS
; (JOIN-in-cycle) back-edge so the p<->q SCC survives opt-mode canonicalization
; (mirrors corecursion_1's ping:pong,add_edge). It exhibits BOTH P6.2 promotion
; discriminator arms:
;   PROMOTE (all producers agree): q's SOLE producer q:p routes p's fields into
;     q, and lookup:q routes q into lookup -> the classes {lookup.K, p.K, q.K}
;     and {lookup.V, p.V, q.V} form (rep = lookup's field, union-by-min).
;   DO-NOT-PROMOTE (multi-source / co-occurrence -- the F16 trap): p has TWO
;     frozen base producers a and b feeding p.K from DIFFERENT sources, so p.K is
;     NOT head-source-promoted and a.K/b.K stay DISTINCT singletons (a buggy
;     any-producer union would wrongly merge a.K==b.K -- absence from any
;     shared-field line is the byte referee).
; @key rides p/q (P5 declared-key render); a bound #query reads q (a request
; port). The answer is a complete read (full-materialization backend), so this
; .stdout is answer-invariant across all four optimization modes; the .region
; sidecar pins the appended rule/shared-field block per mode.
#message base_a(u64 K, u64 V).
#message base_b(u64 K, u64 V).
#message edge(u64 X, u64 V).
#message out_pair(u64 K, u64 V).

#local a(u64 K, u64 V).
#local b(u64 K, u64 V).
#local p(u64 K, u64 V) @key(K).
#local q(u64 K, u64 V) @key(K).

a(K, V) : base_a(K, V).
b(K, V) : base_b(K, V).

q(K, V) : p(K, V).
p(K, V) : q(K, X), edge(X, V).
p(K, V) : a(K, V).
p(K, V) : b(K, V).

out_pair(K, V) : q(K, V).
#query lookup(bound u64 K, free u64 V) : q(K, V).
